hundred-thousand dollars ($500,000) in federal funds from all sources are expended, the
Budget(OMB)CircularA-133.
11. CONFIDENTIALITY. Nothing in this Contract shall be deemed to require the parties to
release any information that is considered confidential by state or federal law.
12. INDEMNIFICATION. Each party agrees to be responsible for any losses, claims,
damages, injuries, demands and causes of action resulting from that party's negligence.
The City does hereby reserve all immunities and defenses provided under the WGCA.
13. CERTIFICATION REGARDING DISBARMENT AND SUSPENSION.By signing this
Contract, the City certifies to the best of its knowledge and belief that it and its principles
are not presently debarred, suspended, proposed for debarment, declared ineligible, or
voluntarily excluded from participation in this transaction by anyfederal department or
agency.
14. EQUIPMENT. If the City uses grant funds under this Contract to purchase any piece
equipment and the Contract is terminated for breach, the piece of equipment shallbe
returned to the LCCPwithin thirty (30) days following termination of this Contract. All
purchases remain property of LCCP and return may be requested.
